      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{651ee4c59bd9ae5010c127e1|full_name}Yes, that’s right.\n\nIt’s the permission to kick people who enter an instance.\n\nI agree that, in principle, kick permissions might belong only to moderators.\n\nHowever, if regular members are allowed to create instances,\n\nthey also need the ability to kick trolls who join those instances.\n\nOtherwise, when creating a world as a public instance, it becomes very easy for it to be griefed.\n\nThis has actually happened before, and it caused real problems.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
